{"id": "EUVD-2026-96591", "enisaUuid": "5db9660d-7dda-3bcb-bce5-2fa966cd88aa", "description": "JeecgBoot through 3.9.5 contains a missing authorization vulnerability in the SystemApiController updateAvatar handler that allows any authenticated user to change other users' avatars. Low-privileged attackers can send PUT requests with a target user id and an arbitrary value, such as an attacker-controlled image URL, to replace administrators' avatars.", "datePublished": "2026-10-10T21:49:40", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-18T12:03:16", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/AnkesKasty/cve-request-poc/blob/a7b6d1423555812d8efa26c91c5d0683164b31e5/JeecgBoot/poc_sys_api_update_avatar.py", "https://github.com/jeecgboot/JeecgBoot/blob/e3b9dc0aefe1943d9772b026f64ed671a7c82802/jeecg-boot/jeecg-module-system/jeecg-system-biz/src/main/java/org/jeecg/modules/api/controller/SystemApiController.java#L830-L833", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/jeecgboot-through-3.9.5-missing-authorization-via-sys-api-updateavatar"], "aliases": ["GHSA-w99x-m7g5-9xgv", "CVE-2026-108652"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "ccb0fa40-4ba1-32b0-b889-7bb37965a370", "product": {"name": "JeecgBoot", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.9.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b7816c94-09bf-3209-b18d-fd1ad357cd6f", "vendor": {"name": "jeecgboot"}}], "isExploited": false}